-- The rest of MCBA Season XIV, from MyStatsOnline.
--
-- The season was imported part-played and had not been brought forward since.
-- Two things were behind: twenty games were missing outright, from the 24th of
-- September to the 5th of October, and eight more were already here with no
-- score on them. Nothing we held disagreed with the source - every difference
-- was something absent rather than something wrong - so this only adds.
--
-- The twenty new rows take their sort_order from their position in the
-- source's own schedule, which continues from 75 where ours left off. Clubs
-- are matched by nickname through this season's own team list, the way
-- import-mso-games.mjs does it, because the schedule page writes "Coyotes"
-- where the club is "ALC Coyotes (MIBL)".
--
-- The box scores are generated per game by scripts/import-one-boxscore.mjs,
-- which is the one that touches only the game named on its command line. Each
-- block clears that game's own line scores and stat rows first, so applying
-- this twice lands in the same place rather than doubling anything. It also
-- sets each final score from the line score's own run totals, which is why the
-- twenty rows go in with no score and get one a few statements later.
--
-- Two games have no box score on the source at all - only a result - so they
-- are scored by hand at the end: Beavers at Samurai on the 30th of September
-- and Samurai at the Coyotes on the 4th of October. They will show a result
-- and no detail, which is what the source has.
--
-- Innings pitched arrive in baseball notation and the importer converts them
-- to outs over three on the way in, so nothing here repeats what 0074 and 0075
-- had to undo.
--
-- Season totals are not touched. They are rebuilt from these box scores by
-- recomputing the season from /admin/seasons, which has to happen after this.

-- The twenty games the archive had never seen.


-- Box score for game 1956756, generated by scripts/import-one-boxscore.mjs.
-- Scoped to this game only: nothing else in the archive is touched.
DELETE FROM historical_line_scores WHERE game_id = (SELECT id FROM historical_games WHERE source_game_id = '1956756');
DELETE FROM historical_game_stats WHERE game_id = (SELECT id FROM historical_games WHERE source_game_id = '1956756');
UPDATE historical_games SET away_score = 6, home_score = 4 WHERE source_game_id = '1956756';

